  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Simulate Chunked Prefill Scheduling** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef inference_chunked_prefill_scheduling(requests: list, max_tokens_per_batch: int = 4) -> list:\n    reqs = [{'id': r['id'], 'p': r['prompt_tokens_remaining'], 'd': r['decode_tokens_remaining']} for r in requests]\n    history = []\n    while any(r['p'] > 0 or r['d'] > 0 for r in reqs):\n        budget = max_tokens_per_batch\n        ops = []\n        for r in reqs:\n            if r['p'] == 0 and r['d'] > 0 and budget > 0:\n                r['d'] -= 1; budget -= 1\n                ops.append({'id': r['id'], 'prefill_tokens': 0, 'decode_tokens': 1})\n        for r in reqs:\n            if budget <= 0: break\n            if r['p'] > 0:\n                chunk = min(budget, r['p'])\n                r['p'] -= chunk; budget -= chunk\n                ops.append({'id': r['id'], 'prefill_tokens': chunk, 'decode_tokens': 0})\n        history.append(ops)\n    return history\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
